.postgres_data
.git
__pycache__
venv
.env

# Training artifacts. home-ubuntu doubles as the YOLO training box and the
# production build host, so without these the web image bakes in ~3.5GB of
# checkpoints and datasets that no deployment ever reads (measured 2026-08-05:
# an 8GB build context producing a 12.3GB image).
runs/
data/go4_*
/yolo*.pt

# Calibration/experiment data. `superpowers/` is track documents plus the raw self-play
# checkpoints they cite -- 6.6GB on home-ubuntu as of 2026-08-20, growing every batch.
# Nothing under `katrain/` reads it at runtime (grep: zero hits outside the JS bundle dir),
# and the derived summaries the docs actually need are committed as small .jsonl.gz.
# Measured: without this, `COPY . /app` spends minutes on the copy alone and the image
# grows by the full size of whatever calibration ran that day.
superpowers/
